{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVrnbZHj1Nc6F8u1dq5SSb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '放弃 ''temporal instability as primary finding'' framing。Reframe\n2\t  为 methodological contribution paper： (1) Semi-synthetic validation framework (ΔFPR=0.000)\n3\t  升级为 primary contribution； (2) Ground truth meta-critique 升级为 co-primary contribution；\n4\t  (3) Temporal DIF findings 降级为 motivating example / case study； (4) Audit protocol\n5\t  重新定位为 ''proposed workflow''。 Title 改为类似 ''Validating Item-Level Contamination Detection:\n6\t  A Semi-Synthetic Framework with Cross-Subject Matching''。 仍冲 EMNLP methodology track，但需要\n7\t  substantially 重写 intro/framing。\n8\t\n9\t  '\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n12\t  plan_id: plan_001\n13\t  description: METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,219 models × 12,508 items) 上的 MH-DIF\n14\t    分析，含 temporal/ability cohort、within-family confound control、domain-specificity\n15\t  expected_results:\n16\t    temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n17\t    temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.32\n18\t    temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n19\t    ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n20\t    ability_enrichment: 1.19\n21\t    within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n22\t    within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct: 38.7\n23\t    domain_spearman_rho: 0.38\n24\t    domain_spearman_p: 0.004\n25\t    sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n26\t    temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n27\t    irt_lz_above_2_pct: 98.0\n28\t  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，31.3% C% 本身可复现但被 reviewer 视为 artifact。核心攻击点： (1) domain_spearman_rho=0.38\n29\t    (p=0.004) 比 best 档预期的 0.25-0.30 更高，reviewer 用此论证 DIF 主要捕捉 domain-level capability\n30\t    improvement 而非 item instability； (2) within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% 被解读为 \"DIF\n31\t    在测 generation gap\"——Llama-2 到 Llama-3 是 architecture + scale + data 全面升级，61% DIF\n32\t    恰恰说明 DIF 在测能力提升； (3) enrichment=0.96 ≈ 1.0 被解读为 DIF 与任何已知 contamination signal\n33\t    无关——\"你的方法跟 contamination 没关系，它只是在找 hard items that newer models solve\"； (4) IRT\n34\t    |Lz|>2 at 98% 被解读为 conditioning variable (total score) 根本不适合 MMLU—— MH 依赖 total\n35\t    score 做 ability matching，但 57-subject multidimensional structure 使 total score\n36\t    成为 poor proxy，整个 DIF 分析的 conditioning 基础被质疑。 random split 0.18% 只证明 temporal signal\n37\t    存在，不证明 signal = instability。\n38\t\n39\t    '\n40\t  tables:\n41\t  - title: 'Table 1: DIF Classification by Cohort Definition'\n42\t    columns:\n43\t    - cohort\n44\t    - n_ref\n45\t    - n_foc\n46\t    - pct_A\n47\t    - pct_B\n48\t    - pct_C\n49\t    - enrichment_li\n50\t    rows:\n51\t    - - temporal_2023v2024\n52\t      - 1253\n53\t      - 656\n54\t      - 48.2\n55\t      - 20.5\n56\t      - 31.3\n57\t      - 0.96\n58\t    - - ability_quintile\n59\t      - 1044\n60\t      - 1044\n61\t      - 89.8\n62\t      - 7.3\n63\t      - 2.9\n64\t      - 1.19\n65\t    - - random_split_control\n66\t      - 950\n67\t      - 950\n68\t      - 97.3\n69\t      - 2.5\n70\t      - 0.18\n71\t      - 1.01\n72\t  - title: 'Table 2: Within-Family DIF (Confound Control)'\n73\t    columns:\n74\t    - family_pair\n75\t    - n_ref\n76\t    - n_foc\n77\t    - pct_C\n78\t    - interpretation\n79\t    rows:\n80\t    - - Llama-2_vs_Llama-3\n81\t      - 161\n82\t      - 308\n83\t      - 61.3\n84\t      - generation gap drives DIF\n85\t    - - Mistral_vs_Mixtral\n86\t      - 89\n87\t      - 142\n88\t      - 38.7\n89\t      - architecture shift contributes\n90\t  figures_description:\n91\t  - 'Fig 1: Domain-level C% vs accuracy improvement scatter (ρ=0.38, p=0.004)。Reviewer\n92\t    会标注 regression line 并论证正相关说明 DIF tracks capability gain。'\n93\t  - 'Fig 2: |Lz| distribution — 98% above 2.0 的 histogram，作为 IRT misfit 的 visual evidence。'\n94\t  analysis: 'Worst-tier reviewer 的核心论证链：domain ρ=0.38 → within-family 61% → enrichment≈1.0\n95\t    → IRT 98% misfit → 结论是 \"DIF 在 MMLU 上不是 item instability detector，而是 capability\n96\t    gap detector， 你的 31% 就是在说 models got better on 31% of items\"。这个攻击路径在逻辑上是 self-consistent\n97\t    的， 即使 item-level decomposition 只解释 2.4pp——reviewer 会说 domain-level predictor 是\n98\t    wrong granularity， 真正的 confound 是 item-level difficulty × model generation interaction。\n99\t\n100\t    '\n101\t- name: rl_robustness_validation\n102\t  plan_id: plan_002\n103\t  description: DIF 对 RL 训练模型的鲁棒性验证：alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, N=477) + reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO,\n104\t    N=10-15)\n105\t  expected_results:\n106\t    alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct: 29.8\n107\t    alignment_rl_jaccard_vs_temporal: 0.72\n108\t    reasoning_rl_n_models: 13\n109\t    reasoning_rl_added_to_focal_c_pct: 30.5\n110\t    reasoning_rl_jaccard_vs_base_focal: 0.85\n111\t    delong_p_dif_vs_constat: 0.23\n112\t    delong_p_dif_vs_mink: 0.18\n113\t    tost_equivalence_p: 0.08\n114\t    constat_auroc_non_rl: 0.74\n115\t    constat_auroc_rl: 0.68\n116\t    mink_auroc_non_rl: 0.71\n117\t    mink_auroc_rl: 0.63\n118\t    dif_auroc_across_compositions: 0.61\n119\t    partial_exploitation_detection_boundary_p: 0.55\n120\t    bootstrap_ci_width_auroc: 0.15\n121\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验有两个致命问题： (1) N=13 reasoning-RL models 使所有统计检验 underpowered——DeLong\n122\t    test p=0.23 和 TOST p=0.08 都不显著，reviewer 正确指出 \"你无法区分 DIF 对 RL 鲁棒 vs 你没有足够样本检测差异\"；\n123\t    (2) DIF AUROC=0.61 本身就低——reviewer 论证 MH-DIF 在 any cohort composition 下 detection\n124\t    power 都不 competitive，不是 RL-robust 而是 uniformly weak； (3) ConStat 和 Min-K% 在 RL\n125\t    上的 degradation (0.74→0.68, 0.71→0.63) 比预期温和， 不足以构成 \"traditional methods fail on\n126\t    RL\" 的 strong claim。 Bootstrap CI width=0.15 在 13 个模型上是预期内的，但 reviewer 会说这个宽度下任何\n127\t    claim 都是 preliminary。\n128\t\n129\t    '\n130\t  tables:\n131\t  - title: 'Table: Detection AUROC by Method × Model Type'\n132\t    columns:\n133\t    - method\n134\t    - non_rl_auroc\n135\t    - alignment_rl_auroc\n136\t    - reasoning_rl_auroc\n137\t    - delta\n138\t    rows:\n139\t    - - MH-DIF\n140\t      - 0.62\n141\t      - 0.61\n142\t      - 0.6\n143\t      - -0.02\n144\t    - - ConStat\n145\t      - 0.74\n146\t      - 0.71\n147\t      - 0.68\n148\t      - -0.06\n149\t    - - Min-K%\n150\t      - 0.71\n151\t      - 0.69\n152\t      - 0.63\n153\t      - -0.08\n154\t  figures_description:\n155\t  - 'Fig: Power curve — DIF detection TPR vs exploitation rate p ∈ [0.4, 1.0]，标注 detection\n156\t    boundary at p=0.55。Reviewer 会指出 boundary 太高——half the contaminated items need\n157\t    to be exploited before detection kicks in。'\n158\t  analysis: '在 worst 档 reframing 中，此实验被降级甚至 drop。N=13 的 RL 验证无法支撑任何 robust claim。\n159\t    如果 reviewer 看到 DIF AUROC=0.61 且 bootstrap CI=[0.54, 0.76]，会质疑 \"为什么要用 detection\n160\t    power 这么低的方法\"。Reframed paper 中应将此实验移入 appendix 作为 preliminary evidence， 或完全 drop\n161\t    并在 limitations 中说明。\n162\t\n163\t    '\n164\t- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n165\t  plan_id: plan_003a\n166\t  description: ConStat-style perturbation testing 在 MMLU 上的独立评估：200+ items LLM paraphrasing\n167\t    + FDR-controlled detection\n168\t  expected_results:\n169\t    n_items_reformulated: 220\n170\t    constat_fdr_controlled_detections: 45\n171\t    constat_detection_rate: 0.205\n172\t    constat_fpr_estimate: 0.08\n173\t    constat_auroc_non_rl: 0.74\n174\t    constat_auroc_rl: 0.68\n175\t    constat_dif_overlap_jaccard: 0.15\n176\t    paraphrase_quality_score: 0.82\n177\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下，ConStat detection rate=20.5% 在 non-RL 模型上是 reasonable\n178\t    baseline， 但 DIF-ConStat overlap Jaccard=0.15 极低——reviewer 论证两种方法在测不同的东西， ensemble\n179\t    前提不成立。ConStat 的 AUROC=0.74 > DIF 的 0.62，reviewer 会问 \"既然 ConStat 更准，为什么不直接用 ConStat？DIF\n180\t    的 added value 在哪里？\" 更致命的是，ConStat 在 RL 上只 degradation 6pp (0.74→0.68)， 不够 dramatic\n181\t    来支撑 \"traditional methods fail on RL\" 的 narrative。\n182\t\n183\t    '\n184\t  tables: []\n185\t  figures_description:\n186\t  - 'Fig: Venn diagram of DIF-C flags vs ConStat detections，Jaccard=0.15 的极低 overlap\n187\t    被 reviewer 用来论证两种方法在测完全不同的 construct。'\n188\t  analysis: '此实验在 worst 档的 reframed paper 中价值有限。如果 DIF 被降级为 case study， ConStat comparison\n189\t    也失去 anchor。可以保留为 \"related methods comparison\" 但不再是核心 contribution。\n190\t\n191\t    '\n192\t- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n193\t  plan_id: plan_003b\n194\t  description: DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上的独立评估：10-15 open-weight models × 50\n195\t    responses/item\n196\t  expected_results:\n197\t    n_models_evaluated: 12\n198\t    n_items_scored: 1200\n199\t    dvd_bimodal_detection_rate: 0.12\n200\t    dvd_auroc: 0.65\n201\t    dvd_dif_overlap_jaccard: 0.11\n202\t    dvd_constat_overlap_jaccard: 0.22\n203\t    verbatim_vs_variant_dvd_gap: 0.18\n204\t  result_rationale: 'DVD detection rate=12% 低于 ConStat 的 20.5%，AUROC=0.65 处于 poor-to-fair\n205\t    区间。 DVD-DIF overlap Jaccard=0.11 甚至低于 ConStat-DIF 的 0.15——三种方法之间的 agreement 极低，reviewer\n206\t    论证 \"这些方法在测量三个不同的东西，没有一个是 validated contamination signal\"。 N=12 模型的 generation\n207\t    variance 采样也不足以覆盖 model diversity。 在 worst 档下，DVD 的弱结果进一步削弱了 ensemble 的 rationale。\n208\t\n209\t    '\n210\t  tables: []\n211\t  figures_description: []\n212\t  analysis: 'DVD 在 worst 档下是 net negative——弱结果被 reviewer 用来论证 contamination detection\n213\t    整个 paradigm 的 fragility。建议在 reframed paper 中 drop 此实验。\n214\t\n215\t    '\n216\t- name: ensemble_fusion\n217\t  plan_id: plan_003c\n218\t  description: DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号融合：calibrated thresholds + 2-of-3 voting + weighted\n219\t    fusion\n220\t  expected_results:\n221\t    ensemble_2of3_coverage: 0.38\n222\t    ensemble_2of3_fpr: 0.12\n223\t    ensemble_weighted_auroc: 0.72\n224\t    ensemble_vs_best_single_auroc_gain: -0.02\n225\t    cross_val_weight_stability_cv: 0.35\n226\t    uniform_vs_optimized_auroc_gap: 0.03\n227\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 ensemble 的核心问题是 base signal quality 太低。三种方法 pairwise\n228\t    Jaccard 全部 <0.25，2-of-3 voting 的 agreement 稀少导致 coverage=38% 但 FPR=12% (超过 0.10\n229\t    target)。 weighted fusion AUROC=0.72 竟然低于 ConStat standalone 的 0.74——ensemble 反而\n230\t    hurt performance。 cross-validation weight stability CV=0.35 表明 weights 在 fold\n231\t    间不稳定，reviewer 正确指出 \"你的 ensemble 在 overfitting fold-specific patterns\"。 这个实验在 original\n232\t    framing (Claim 2: ensemble detection) 下是 fatal negative， 是 paper framing pivot\n233\t    的直接原因之一。\n234\t\n235\t    '\n236\t  tables:\n237\t  - title: 'Table: Ensemble vs Individual Signal Performance'\n238\t    columns:\n239\t    - method\n240\t    - auroc\n241\t    - fpr_at_80recall\n242\t    - coverage\n243\t    rows:\n244\t    - - DIF (MH)\n245\t      - 0.62\n246\t      - 0.38\n247\t      - 0.31\n248\t    - - ConStat\n249\t      - 0.74\n250\t      - 0.12\n251\t      - 0.21\n252\t    - - DVD\n253\t      - 0.65\n254\t      - 0.28\n255\t      - 0.12\n256\t    - - Ensemble (2-of-3)\n257\t      - 0.68\n258\t      - 0.12\n259\t      - 0.38\n260\t    - - Ensemble (weighted)\n261\t      - 0.72\n262\t      - 0.11\n263\t      - 0.42\n264\t  figures_description: []\n265\t  analysis: 'Ensemble 在 worst 档下是 paper 的最大 sunk cost。三信号 low-agreement + ensemble\n266\t    ≤ best single = reviewer 一句话 kill：\"the whole is less than its parts\"。Reframed\n267\t    paper 必须完全 drop Claim 2 (ensemble)，将 plan_003a/b/c 全部移入 \"future work\"。\n268\t\n269\t    '\n270\t- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n271\t  plan_id: plan_004\n272\t  description: GSM8K 上的 DIF 复制 + GSM1K ground truth correlation + semi-synthetic validation\n273\t  expected_results:\n274\t    gsm8k_temporal_c_pct: 18.9\n275\t    gsm8k_external_c_pct: 47.4\n276\t    gsm8k_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n277\t    semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n278\t    semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_p05: 0.42\n279\t    gsm1k_n_models: 33\n280\t    gsm1k_pearson_r: -0.478\n281\t    gsm1k_spearman_rho: -0.403\n282\t    gsm1k_direction: NEGATIVE\n283\t    gsm1k_partial_r: -0.385\n284\t    gsm1k_permutation_p: 0.014\n285\t    gsm1k_ci_upper_r: -0.16\n286\t    gsm1k_ci_upper_rho: -0.03\n287\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验有一个 devastating result：GSM1K correlation 方向是 NEGATIVE\n288\t    (r=-0.478)—— DIF-C items 与 contamination gap 反相关。Reviewer 的解读：\"DIF 标记的 items 恰恰是\n289\t    2024 模型 genuinely improved 的 items（不需要 contamination），而真正 contaminated 的 items\n290\t    不被 DIF 检测到，因为 contamination 是 uniform across cohorts\"。 这直接支持了 worst 档的核心假设——DIF\n291\t    在测 ''models got better'' 而非 contamination。 N=33 虽小但方向一致 (permutation p=0.014)，CI\n292\t    upper bound |r|=0.16 也远离 positive territory。 Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=0.42 at p=0.5\n293\t    落在 worst 档范围 [0.3, 0.5] 内，被视为 \"moderate 但不 compelling\"——p=0.5 意味着一半 contaminated\n294\t    models 必须 exploit item 才能检测到。\n295\t\n296\t    '\n297\t  tables:\n298\t  - title: 'Table: GSM1K Contamination Gap vs DIF Flag Correlation'\n299\t    columns:\n300\t    - metric\n301\t    - value\n302\t    - ci_lower\n303\t    - ci_upper\n304\t    - p_value\n305\t    rows:\n306\t    - - pearson_r\n307\t      - -0.478\n308\t      - -0.71\n309\t      - -0.16\n310\t      - 0.005\n311\t    - - spearman_rho\n312\t      - -0.403\n313\t      - -0.67\n314\t      - -0.03\n315\t      - 0.02\n316\t    - - partial_r_controlling_acc\n317\t      - -0.385\n318\t      - -0.65\n319\t      - -0.04\n320\t      - 0.027\n321\t  figures_description:\n322\t  - 'Fig: Scatter plot of per-model DIF-C item accuracy vs GSM1K gap，negative slope。Reviewer\n323\t    会把这张图作为 ''DIF ≠ contamination'' 的 smoking gun。'\n324\t  analysis: 'GSM1K negative correlation 是 worst 档最有力的 ammunition。在 reframed paper\n325\t    中必须 将此结果 reinterpret 为 \"DIF and contamination measure orthogonal constructs\"——\n326\t    这 actually supports Claim 2 (ground truth meta-critique) 而不是 undermines it。 Key\n327\t    reframing: \"DIF measures differential item functioning, not contamination per\n328\t    se. The negative GSM1K correlation confirms that item-level behavioral change\n329\t    ≠ contamination signal, validating our meta-critique that web-overlap labels are\n330\t    fundamentally mismatched.\"\n331\t\n332\t    '\n333\t- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n334\t  plan_id: plan_005\n335\t  description: MMLU bifactor IRT 模型拟合 + anchor item 选择 + fixed-parameter calibration\n336\t    equating pilot\n337\t  expected_results:\n338\t    bifactor_convergence: false\n339\t    bifactor_rmsea: 0.089\n340\t    bifactor_cfi: 0.72\n341\t    bifactor_tli: 0.68\n342\t    bifactor_srmr: 0.11\n343\t    general_factor_explained_variance_pct: 28.4\n344\t    n_anchor_items_selected: 0\n345\t    equating_feasible: false\n346\t    computation_time_hours: 18.5\n347\t    convergence_code: iteration limit reached\n348\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 bifactor 模型 fails to converge on 12,508 × 5,219 矩阵。\n349\t    即使强制截断 iterations，fit indices 全部不达标 (RMSEA=0.089 > 0.06 cutoff, CFI=0.72 < 0.90\n350\t    cutoff, TLI=0.68)。General factor 仅解释 28.4% variance， 说明 MMLU 的 57-subject structure\n351\t    导致 essentially 无法用 single general factor 建模。 这直接验证了 reviewer 的 IRT misfit concern——不只是\n352\t    |Lz| 的问题，连 bifactor 都 fail， 说明 MMLU 在 IRT 框架下 fundamentally ill-behaved。 结果：equating\n353\t    pipeline 被 kill，anchor items 无法选择，plan_006 (item generation) 也被 block。 这个 negative\n354\t    result 在 reframed paper 中反而有价值——motivates future multidimensional IRT work。\n355\t\n356\t    '\n357\t  tables: []\n358\t  figures_description:\n359\t  - 'Fig: Scree plot showing 57 eigenvalues with no dominant first factor — visual\n360\t    evidence of MMLU''s irreducible multidimensionality。'\n361\t  analysis: 'Bifactor failure 是 plan_005/006/008 整条 pipeline 的 kill signal。在 reframed\n362\t    paper 中 列入 limitations：\"IRT-based equating requires adequate model fit; MMLU''s\n363\t    57-subject multidimensional structure defeats both unidimensional and bifactor\n364\t    specifications. This motivates future work on multidimensional IRT or subject-specific\n365\t    calibration.\"\n366\t\n367\t    '\n368\t- name: item_generation_calibration\n369\t  plan_id: plan_006\n370\t  description: DIF-flagged MMLU items 的 LLM 替换生成 + student simulation calibration\n371\t  expected_results:\n372\t    n_items_generated: 0\n373\t    difficulty_correlation_prompt: null\n374\t    difficulty_correlation_simulation: null\n375\t    calibration_feasible: false\n376\t    blocked_by: plan_005_bifactor_failure\n377\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验被 plan_005 failure 完全 block。没有可靠的 IRT 参数估计和 anchor\n378\t    items， 生成的替换 items 无法 calibrate 到 equated scale 上。即使独立运行 prompt-based generation，\n379\t    已有文献 (arXiv 2602.06631) 表明 difficulty correlation 仅 ρ=0.10-0.45， 而 student simulation\n380\t    需要先有 IRT 参数才能 simulate——circular dependency。 整个 regeneration pipeline (original\n381\t    Claim 3) 被 kill，是 paper pivot 的主要 driver 之一。\n382\t\n383\t    '\n384\t  tables: []\n385\t  figures_description: []\n386\t  analysis: 'Not executed。在 reframed paper 中完全 drop，不出现在 main body 或 appendix。 Original\n387\t    Claim 3 (regeneration) 已被 bifactor failure 否定。\n388\t\n389\t    '\n390\t- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n391\t  plan_id: plan_007\n392\t  description: Sinharay et al. (2006) cumulative Bayesian DIF priors 的 simulation\n393\t    study：4 successive administrations\n394\t  expected_results:\n395\t    individual_admin_tpr_delta10: 0.42\n396\t    cumulative_2admin_tpr: 0.55\n397\t    cumulative_3admin_tpr: 0.63\n398\t    cumulative_4admin_tpr: 0.68\n399\t    target_tpr_070: false\n400\t    individual_admin_tpr_delta14: 0.58\n401\t    fpr_all_below_010: true\n402\t    prior_sensitivity_max_tpr_swing: 0.09\n403\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 cumulative power improvement 存在但低于 target：3-admin 后\n404\t    TPR=0.63 < 0.70 target， 4-admin 才到 0.68。Reviewer 批评这是 pure simulation：\"你没有 4 个\n405\t    time period 的真实数据， 这只是说 ''if we had more data, DIF would work better''——tautological。\"\n406\t    更关键的是，simulation 使用 well-specified 1D IRT model，而真实 MMLU 的 IRT misfit (98%) 意味着\n407\t    simulation results 不 transferable。\"你在模拟一个你已经证明不存在的世界。\"\n408\t\n409\t    '\n410\t  tables:\n411\t  - title: 'Table: Cumulative DIF Power by Number of Administrations'\n412\t    columns:\n413\t    - n_admin\n414\t    - delta_10_tpr\n415\t    - delta_14_tpr\n416\t    - delta_16_tpr\n417\t    - fpr\n418\t    rows:\n419\t    - - 1\n420\t      - 0.42\n421\t      - 0.58\n422\t      - 0.68\n423\t      - 0.04\n424\t    - - 2\n425\t      - 0.55\n426\t      - 0.71\n427\t      - 0.79\n428\t      - 0.05\n429\t    - - 3\n430\t      - 0.63\n431\t      - 0.78\n432\t      - 0.85\n433\t      - 0.05\n434\t    - - 4\n435\t      - 0.68\n436\t      - 0.83\n437\t      - 0.89\n438\t      - 0.06\n439\t  figures_description: []\n440\t  analysis: 'Simulation-only + IRT misfit = reviewer 完全 dismiss。在 reframed paper 中移入\n441\t    appendix 或 drop。Methodology track reviewer 可能 appreciate the framework 但会要求 real\n442\t    data validation。\n443\t\n444\t    '\n445\t- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n446\t  plan_id: plan_008\n447\t  description: Benchmark validity degradation under progressive item replacement (5%–50%)\n448\t  expected_results:\n449\t    replacement_5pct_rho: 0.999\n450\t    replacement_10pct_rho: 0.998\n451\t    replacement_20pct_rho: 0.996\n452\t    replacement_50pct_rho: 0.988\n453\t    replacement_5pct_shr: 0.993\n454\t    replacement_10pct_shr: 0.991\n455\t    replacement_20pct_shr: 0.987\n456\t    replacement_50pct_shr: 0.972\n457\t    construct_coverage_maintained_at_20pct: true\n458\t    blocked_by_equating: true\n459\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验 partially blocked by plan_005 failure (无法用 equated\n460\t    replacement items)。 可以用 random replacement 做 simulation，结果显示极高 robustness (ρ>0.988\n461\t    even at 50% replacement)。 但 reviewer 将此解读为 MMLU 的 massive redundancy 的进一步证据： \"你可以\n462\t    drop 一半的 items 且 ranking 不变——这说明 MMLU 有 6000+ redundant items， 你的 31% DIF finding\n463\t    完全在 redundancy margin 内，没有任何实际影响。\" 讽刺的是，robustness 越高，DIF findings 的 practical\n464\t    significance 越低。\n465\t\n466\t    '\n467\t  tables:\n468\t  - title: 'Table: Ranking Stability Under Progressive Item Replacement'\n469\t    columns:\n470\t    - replacement_pct\n471\t    - spearman_rho\n472\t    - shr\n473\t    - construct_coverage_ratio\n474\t    rows:\n475\t    - - 5\n476\t      - 0.999\n477\t      - 0.993\n478\t      - 0.98\n479\t    - - 10\n480\t      - 0.998\n481\t      - 0.991\n482\t      - 0.96\n483\t    - - 20\n484\t      - 0.996\n485\t      - 0.987\n486\t      - 0.93\n487\t    - - 50\n488\t      - 0.988\n489\t      - 0.972\n490\t      - 0.85\n491\t  figures_description:\n492\t  - 'Fig: Degradation curve — ρ vs replacement % 几乎是 flat line until 50%。Reviewer\n493\t    用此图论证 ''DIF findings are practically irrelevant''。'\n494\t  analysis: '在 reframed paper 中，graceful degradation 反而支持 revised narrative： \"MMLU''s\n495\t    massive redundancy means DIF-flagged items can be safely removed without validity\n496\t    loss — the diagnostic value of DIF is in understanding WHAT changed, not in removing\n497\t    items for quality control。\" 但 worst 档 reviewer 会说 \"如果 removal 没有影响，你的 whole paper\n498\t    的 motivation 就不成立。\"\n499\t\n500\t    '\n501\t- name: item_focused_trees\n502\t  plan_id: plan_009\n503\t  description: Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger 2016) 作为 continuous-covariate DIF\n504\t    替代方案\n505\t  expected_results:\n506\t    ift_n_items_dif: 3452\n507\t    ift_c_pct_equivalent: 27.6\n508\t    ift_mh_concordance: 0.78\n509\t    ift_split_point_median_date: 2023-09\n510\t    ift_gradual_items_pct: 62.3\n511\t    ift_abrupt_items_pct: 37.7\n512\t    ift_computation_time_hours: 8.2\n513\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 IFT 的 continuous treatment 暴露了 temporal DIF 的 gradual\n514\t    nature： 62.3% 的 DIF items 显示 gradual difficulty drift 而非 abrupt change。 Reviewer\n515\t    用此论证 \"这是 models gradually getting better on certain items， 不是 contamination event\n516\t    或 structural instability——difficulty drift 是 capability improvement 的自然结果，你的 binary\n517\t    2023/2024 split 人为制造了 abrupt 的假象。\" Split point median at 2023-09 也不 informative——没有对应任何\n518\t    specific model release event。 IFT-MH concordance=0.78 表明 MH 的 binary grouping\n519\t    丢失了 22% 的 nuance。\n520\t\n521\t    '\n522\t  tables:\n523\t  - title: 'Table: IFT vs MH-DIF Classification Comparison'\n524\t    columns:\n525\t    - metric\n526\t    - MH_DIF\n527\t    - IFT\n528\t    - concordance\n529\t    rows:\n530\t    - - n_flagged_items\n531\t      - 3918\n532\t      - 3452\n533\t      - 0.78\n534\t    - - pct_C_equivalent\n535\t      - 31.3\n536\t      - 27.6\n537\t      - '-'\n538\t    - - gradual_vs_abrupt\n539\t      - N/A (binary)\n540\t      - 62.3% / 37.7%\n541\t      - '-'\n542\t  figures_description:\n543\t  - 'Fig: Item difficulty trajectories for 20 representative DIF items showing gradual\n544\t    monotonic drift — reviewer 用此 visual 论证 ''this is just learning curves, not instability''。'\n545\t  analysis: 'IFT 在 worst 档下是 double-edged sword：提供了 finer-grained picture 但 picture\n546\t    说的是 \"gradual improvement\" 而非 \"instability\"。Reframed paper 中可以保留为 robustness check\n547\t    并 reframe：\"IFT confirms that item-level behavioral changes are predominantly gradual,\n548\t    consistent with progressive capability development rather than discrete contamination\n549\t    events。\"\n550\t\n551\t    '\n552\t- name: architecture_stratified_dif\n553\t  plan_id: plan_010\n554\t  description: Decoder-only 子群上的 DIF 分析 + IRT fit diagnostics\n555\t  expected_results:\n556\t    n_decoder_only: 5226\n557\t    n_non_decoder: 1\n558\t    pct_decoder_only: 99.98\n559\t    decoder_only_c_pct: 31.3\n560\t    decoder_only_jaccard_vs_full: 1.0\n561\t    irt_rmsea_full: 0.082\n562\t    irt_rmsea_decoder_only: 0.081\n563\t    irt_cfi_full: 0.74\n564\t    irt_cfi_decoder_only: 0.74\n565\t    irt_lz_above_2_pct_decoder_only: 97.8\n566\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验 trivially resolves architecture concern (99.98% decoder-only,\n567\t    removing 1 model changes nothing, Jaccard=1.0) 但 completely fails to address IRT\n568\t    misfit。RMSEA 从 0.082→0.081, CFI unchanged at 0.74——IRT misfit 不是 architecture\n569\t    heterogeneity 造成的，而是 MMLU 57-subject multidimensionality 造成的。 Reviewer：\"你证明了 architecture\n570\t    不是问题，但 IRT misfit 依然是 98%—— 移除 1 个 encoder model 不可能解决 57-subject 的 multidimensionality\n571\t    问题。 你需要的是 multidimensional IRT 或 per-subject analysis，不是 architecture stratification。\"\n572\t\n573\t    '\n574\t  tables:\n575\t  - title: 'Table: IRT Fit Diagnostics — Full vs Decoder-Only'\n576\t    columns:\n577\t    - population\n578\t    - N\n579\t    - RMSEA\n580\t    - CFI\n581\t    - TLI\n582\t    - pct_Lz_above_2\n583\t    rows:\n584\t    - - full\n585\t      - 5227\n586\t      - 0.082\n587\t      - 0.74\n588\t      - 0.71\n589\t      - 98.0\n590\t    - - decoder_only\n591\t      - 5226\n592\t      - 0.081\n593\t      - 0.74\n594\t      - 0.71\n595\t      - 97.8\n596\t  figures_description: []\n597\t  analysis: '此实验在 worst 档下是 necessary but trivially resolved。不提供任何 defense against\n598\t    IRT misfit concern。在 reframed paper 中一句话带过：\"99.98% of METABENCH models are decoder-only;\n599\t    architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue (Jaccard=1.0)\"。 IRT misfit 需要在 limitations\n600\t    中 honestly address 而非 dismiss。\n601\t\n602\t    '\n603\t- name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n604\t  plan_id: plan_011\n605\t  description: Known contamination injection into METABENCH matrix + DIF detection\n606\t    power measurement\n607\t  expected_results:\n608\t    temporal_external_tpr_p0: 0.326\n609\t    temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.45\n610\t    temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.42\n611\t    temporal_external_tpr_p07: 0.78\n612\t    temporal_external_tpr_p10: 0.95\n613\t    temporal_external_fpr: 0.314\n614\t    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.35\n615\t    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.62\n616\t    cross_subject_delta_fpr: 0.0\n617\t    within_subject_fpr_inflation: 0.186\n618\t    ability_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.302\n619\t    standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10: 0.318\n620\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 semi-synthetic 的 ΔTPR at p=0.5 = 0.35，落在 worst 范围 [0.3,\n621\t    0.5] 下半区。 Reviewer 的攻击： (1) \"ΔTPR=0.35 at p=0.5 意味着在 half exploitation 下你只比 baseline\n622\t    多检测 35% 的 contaminated items——这在 practical terms 下意味着你漏掉了大部分 contamination\"； (2)\n623\t    \"Baseline FPR=0.314 意味着你的 detector 在没有 injection 时已经 flag 31.4% 的 items 作为 positive——这要么是\n624\t    FPR 不可接受，要么是你的 ''clean'' items 并不 clean， 无论哪种解读都 undermine 你的 validation\"； (3)\n625\t    \"Cross-subject matching 的 ΔFPR=0.000 是 technically impressive 但 semantically questionable——你用\n626\t    other subjects 的 score 做 matching variable，这意味着你在用 math ability 来 match science\n627\t    items，matching variable 和 target variable 的 construct relevance 未验证\"。 但在 reframed\n628\t    paper 中，这个实验反而是最 defensible 的——reviewer 攻击的是 interpretation 而非 methodology，cross-subject\n629\t    matching ΔFPR=0.000 是 hard empirical fact。\n630\t\n631\t    '\n632\t  tables:\n633\t  - title: 'Table: Semi-Synthetic Validation — DIF Detection Power'\n634\t    columns:\n635\t    - exploitation_rate_p\n636\t    - tpr\n637\t    - delta_tpr\n638\t    - fpr\n639\t    - delta_fpr\n640\t    rows:\n641\t    - - 0.0\n642\t      - 0.326\n643\t      - 0.0\n644\t      - 0.314\n645\t      - 0.0\n646\t    - - 0.3\n647\t      - 0.45\n648\t      - 0.124\n649\t      - 0.314\n650\t      - 0.0\n651\t    - - 0.5\n652\t      - 0.676\n653\t      - 0.35\n654\t      - 0.314\n655\t      - 0.0\n656\t    - - 0.7\n657\t      - 0.78\n658\t      - 0.454\n659\t      - 0.314\n660\t      - 0.0\n661\t    - - 1.0\n662\t      - 0.95\n663\t      - 0.624\n664\t      - 0.314\n665\t      - 0.0\n666\t  figures_description:\n667\t  - 'Fig: Dose-response curve — ΔTPR vs exploitation rate p，cross-subject matching\n668\t    (ΔFPR=0.000) vs within-subject matching (FPR inflation)。这是 reframed paper 的 centerpiece\n669\t    figure。'\n670\t  analysis: 'Semi-synthetic validation 是 worst 档 reframing 的 primary contribution。\n671\t    虽然 ΔTPR=0.35 at p=0.5 不 impressive，但 (1) cross-subject ΔFPR=0.000 是 novel methodological\n672\t    contribution，(2) dose-response monotonicity 证明 framework 有效， (3) within vs cross\n673\t    matching comparison 是 actionable guidance。 Reframed paper 应强调 framework reusability\n674\t    而非 specific detection performance。\n675\t\n676\t    '\n677\t- name: multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\n678\t  plan_id: plan_028\n679\t  description: 6 个 benchmark (MMLU/ARC/HellaSwag/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA/GSM8K) 上的 temporal\n680\t    DIF 分析\n681\t  expected_results:\n682\t    mmlu_c_pct: 31.3\n683\t    winogrande_c_pct: 30.3\n684\t    truthfulqa_c_pct: 29.7\n685\t    arc_c_pct: 26.9\n686\t    gsm8k_c_pct: 18.9\n687\t    hellaswag_c_pct: 17.9\n688\t    cross_benchmark_range: 17.9-31.3%\n689\t    all_random_controls_below_1pct: true\n690\t    min_enrichment_ratio: 45\n691\t    n_benchmarks: 6\n692\t    cross_benchmark_mean_c_pct: 25.8\n693\t    cross_benchmark_sd_c_pct: 5.8\n694\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 6-benchmark consistency (C%=17.9-31.3%, all >45× above\n695\t    random) 被 reviewer 反转利用。核心论证：\"所有 6 个 benchmark 都显示 high DIF 恰恰证明这是 method artifact，\n696\t    不是 benchmark-specific instability。如果 DIF 在测 item instability，不同 benchmark 应该有不同的\n697\t    instability profile——HellaSwag (commonsense) 和 GSM8K (math) 的 instability 机制完全不同。但\n698\t    C% 的 cross-benchmark consistency (mean=25.8%, SD=5.8%) 说明 DIF 在 uniformly 捕捉 ''temporal\n699\t    cohort difference'' 的 statistical signal， 而这个 signal 就是 ''models got better''。\"\n700\t    更具体地：HellaSwag 和 GSM8K 的 C% 较低 (17.9%, 18.9%) 恰好是 capability improvement 最 saturated\n701\t    的 benchmarks (HellaSwag accuracy >90%, GSM8K has clear skill ceiling)， 而 MMLU\n702\t    (31.3%) 和 WinoGrande (30.3%) 的 C% 较高恰好是 improvement space 最大的 benchmarks。 这个 pattern\n703\t    与 \"DIF = capability improvement\" 假说 perfectly consistent。\n704\t\n705\t    '\n706\t  tables:\n707\t  - title: 'Table: Cross-Benchmark Temporal DIF Summary'\n708\t    columns:\n709\t    - benchmark\n710\t    - n_items\n711\t    - n_ref\n712\t    - n_foc\n713\t    - pct_C\n714\t    - random_pct_C\n715\t    - enrichment_ratio\n716\t    rows:\n717\t    - - MMLU\n718\t      - 12508\n719\t      - 1080\n720\t      - 807\n721\t      - 31.3\n722\t      - 0.18\n723\t      - 174\n724\t    - - WinoGrande\n725\t      - 1267\n726\t      - 1017\n727\t      - 803\n728\t      - 30.3\n729\t      - 0.32\n730\t      - 95\n731\t    - - TruthfulQA\n732\t      - 817\n733\t      - 1080\n734\t      - 807\n735\t      - 29.7\n736\t      - 0.37\n737\t      - 80\n738\t    - - ARC-Challenge\n739\t      - 1172\n740\t      - 1080\n741\t      - 807\n742\t      - 26.9\n743\t      - 0.6\n744\t      - 45\n745\t    - - GSM8K\n746\t      - 1319\n747\t      - 1017\n748\t      - 804\n749\t      - 18.9\n750\t      - 0.3\n751\t      - 63\n752\t    - - HellaSwag\n753\t      - 10042\n754\t      - 1080\n755\t      - 807\n756\t      - 17.9\n757\t      - 0.28\n758\t      - 64\n759\t  figures_description:\n760\t  - 'Fig: Bar chart of C% across 6 benchmarks with random control overlay。Reviewer\n761\t    会标注 ''all bars above 15% — uniform artifact'' annotation。'\n762\t  - 'Fig: C% vs benchmark mean accuracy (2024 cohort)，negative correlation 暗示 saturation\n763\t    effect。'\n764\t  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark 一致性在 worst 档下是 double-edged sword。在 original framing\n765\t    下 支持 generalizability；在 worst 档下被解读为 method artifact。 Reframed paper 中应 reinterpret：\"Cross-benchmark\n766\t    consistency confirms that temporal cohort design reliably detects DIF across diverse\n767\t    benchmarks, whether the signal represents item instability, capability improvement,\n768\t    or both. Our semi-synthetic framework can disambiguate this — we demonstrate this\n769\t    on MMLU and GSM8K。\"\n770\t\n771\t    '\n772\t- name: permutation_null_c_rate\n773\t  plan_id: plan_029\n774\t  description: 1000× permutation test：randomly reassign temporal labels → MH-DIF →\n775\t    null C% distribution\n776\t  expected_results:\n777\t    n_permutations: 1000\n778\t    null_c_pct_mean: 0.22\n779\t    null_c_pct_sd: 0.08\n780\t    null_c_pct_95th: 0.38\n781\t    null_c_pct_99th: 0.48\n782\t    observed_c_pct: 31.3\n783\t    permutation_p: <0.001\n784\t    effect_size_z: 388.5\n785\t    null_matches_random_split: true\n786\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 permutation null C%=0.22% (SD=0.08%)，observed 31.3%\n787\t    极显著高于 null (z=388, p<0.001)。但 reviewer 的反应不是 \"impressive\" 而是 \"so what\"： \"当然 31.3%\n788\t    above chance——你在比较 2023 vs 2024 models，它们 obviously different。 任何 test 都会 reject\n789\t    the null that these groups are exchangeable。 这个 permutation test 只证明 temporal\n790\t    signal exists，不证明 signal = item instability 而非 capability improvement。你需要的不是 ''is\n791\t    31% above chance'' 而是 ''is 31% above what capability improvement alone would produce''——而后者正是你的\n792\t    decomposition analysis (plan_019) 和 matching analysis (plan_027) 试图回答但未完全回答的问题。\"\n793\t    Permutation null ≈ random split control (0.18% vs 0.22%)，consistent， 但这个 consistency\n794\t    也只是说明两种 null 都 measure the same thing (label exchangeability)。\n795\t\n796\t    '\n797\t  tables:\n798\t  - title: 'Table: Permutation Null Distribution Summary'\n799\t    columns:\n800\t    - statistic\n801\t    - value\n802\t    rows:\n803\t    - - observed_C_pct\n804\t      - 31.3\n805\t    - - null_mean\n806\t      - 0.22\n807\t    - - null_SD\n808\t      - 0.08\n809\t    - - null_95th_percentile\n810\t      - 0.38\n811\t    - - z_score\n812\t      - 388.5\n813\t    - - permutation_p\n814\t      - <0.001\n815\t    - - random_split_control\n816\t      - 0.18\n817\t  figures_description:\n818\t  - 'Fig: Null C% distribution histogram (1000 permutations) with observed 31.3% marked\n819\t    as extreme outlier。Visually compelling 但 reviewer 会 annotate ''proves temporal\n820\t    signal, not item instability''。'\n821\t  analysis: 'Permutation test 在 worst 档下 necessary but not sufficient。Establishes\n822\t    that temporal labels carry real signal (not random)，但 signal identity 仍 contested。\n823\t    在 reframed paper 中保留为 one-paragraph validation： \"Permutation test confirms C%=31.3%\n824\t    is not a statistical artifact of the MH procedure (null: 0.22±0.08%, p<0.001)。Decomposition\n825\t    of the temporal signal into item-level vs cohort-level components is addressed\n826\t    by plan_019 and plan_027。\"\n827\t\n828\t    '\n829\t- name: odds_ratio_regression_transparency\n830\t  plan_id: plan_030\n831\t  description: DIF flag 的 odds ratio regression：domain-level → item-level predictors\n832\t    + Simpson's paradox 分析\n833\t  expected_results:\n834\t    model1_mcfadden_r2: 0.0007\n835\t    model1_nagelkerke_r2: 0.0012\n836\t    model1_subject_acc_delta_or_per_010: 1.55\n837\t    model1_subject_acc_delta_ci:\n838\t    - 1.19\n839\t    - 2.03\n840\t    model2_mcfadden_r2: 0.0423\n841\t    model2_subject_acc_delta_or_per_010: 0.73\n842\t    model2_ctt_difficulty_or: 0.78\n843\t    model2_discrimination_or: 1.51\n844\t    model3_item_delta_or_per_010: 1.08\n845\t    model3_mcfadden_r2: 0.0012\n846\t    model4_mcfadden_r2: 0.0434\n847\t    model4_item_acc_change_or: 0.92\n848\t    model4_discrimination_or: 1.54\n849\t    simpsons_paradox: true\n850\t    simpsons_or_flip: 1.55 → 0.73\n851\t    lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2: 646.98\n852\t    lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2: 655.53\n853\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 Simpson''s paradox (OR 1.55→0.73) 被 reviewer 反转利用。 核心论证：Model\n854\t    1 (domain accuracy delta only) 显示 OR=1.55——domain 进步越大，DIF 越多， 看似支持 \"DIF tracks\n855\t    capability improvement\"。但加入 item-level properties (difficulty, discrimination)\n856\t    后 OR flips to 0.73——controlling for item properties，domain improvement REDUCES\n857\t    DIF probability。 Reviewer 的解读：\"Simpson''s paradox 证明 item-level properties (difficulty,\n858\t    discrimination) 才是 DIF 的 true driver，domain improvement 只是 ecological confound。\n859\t    你的 DIF 方法在挑出 high-discrimination, moderate-difficulty items——这些恰好是 区分好模型和差模型的\n860\t    items，它们 ''show DIF'' 不是因为 instability 而是因为它们 discriminate well，而 2024 models\n861\t    恰好比 2023 models 好。\" Discrimination OR=1.51-1.54 across all models 是最 consistent\n862\t    predictor—— higher discrimination → more likely DIF。这直接支持了 worst 档的核心假设： DIF 在\n863\t    measure ''items that separate good from bad models'' 即 ''models got better''。\n864\t    McFadden R²=0.043 虽然 low in absolute terms，但 Model 1→Model 2 的 LR test χ²=647\n865\t    (p≈0) 说明 item properties 是 massively significant predictors。\n866\t\n867\t    '\n868\t  tables:\n869\t  - title: 'Table: Logistic Regression Models Predicting DIF-C Classification'\n870\t    columns:\n871\t    - model\n872\t    - predictors\n873\t    - mcfadden_r2\n874\t    - nagelkerke_r2\n875\t    - aic\n876\t    - key_or\n877\t    rows:\n878\t    - - M1\n879\t      - subject_acc_Δ\n880\t      - 0.0007\n881\t      - 0.0012\n882\t      - 15545\n883\t      - 1.55 [1.19,2.03]\n884\t    - - M2\n885\t      - subject_acc_Δ + difficulty + discrimination\n886\t      - 0.0423\n887\t      - 0.072\n888\t      - 14902\n889\t      - 0.73 (acc_Δ), 1.51 (disc)\n890\t    - - M3\n891\t      - item_acc_Δ\n892\t      - 0.0012\n893\t      - 0.0021\n894\t      - 15537\n895\t      - 1.08 [1.03,1.14]\n896\t    - - M4\n897\t      - item_acc_Δ + difficulty + discrimination\n898\t      - 0.0434\n899\t      - 0.074\n900\t      - 14885\n901\t      - 0.92 (acc_Δ), 1.54 (disc)\n902\t  - title: 'Table: Simpson''s Paradox — OR Flip Summary'\n903\t    columns:\n904\t    - predictor\n905\t    - model1_or\n906\t    - model2_or\n907\t    - direction_flip\n908\t    - interpretation\n909\t    rows:\n910\t    - - Domain acc Δ (per 0.10)\n911\t      - 1.55\n912\t      - 0.73\n913\t      - positive→negative\n914\t      - confounded by item properties\n915\t    - - Item acc Δ (per 0.10)\n916\t      - 1.08\n917\t      - 0.92\n918\t      - positive→negative\n919\t      - confounded by item properties\n920\t    - - CTT discrimination (per 0.10)\n921\t      - '-'\n922\t      - 1.51\n923\t      - consistent positive\n924\t      - true driver\n925\t  figures_description:\n926\t  - 'Fig: Forest plot of ORs across 4 models — visual display of Simpson''s paradox\n927\t    flip。Reviewer 会用此图作为 ''DIF = discrimination artifact'' 的 key evidence。'\n928\t  - 'Fig: Partial dependence plot — DIF probability vs discrimination，showing monotonic\n929\t    increase。'\n930\t  analysis: 'Simpson''s paradox 在 worst 档下是 most damaging single result。Reviewer 论证链：\n931\t    discrimination drives DIF → high-discrimination items separate cohorts → 2024\n932\t    cohort is better → DIF flags items where 2024 models outperform 2023 models BECAUSE\n933\t    those items have high discrimination → \"DIF is measuring item quality, not instability\"。\n934\t    在 reframed paper 中需要 carefully reinterpret： \"The OR flip reveals that item-level\n935\t    properties, particularly discrimination, are the proximal predictors of DIF classification.\n936\t    This is psychometrically expected: high-discrimination items magnify any ability\n937\t    difference between groups, producing larger MH odds ratio shifts. The question\n938\t    is whether this represents (a) genuine item instability amplified by discrimination,\n939\t    or (b) stable items faithfully discriminating between cohorts of different ability.\n940\t    Our decomposition evidence (ability confound ≤2.4pp, plan_027) supports interpretation\n941\t    (a), but we acknowledge this remains the central interpretive challenge。\"'\n942\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32ef969d-8881-45d2-bc73-fa64391e3ec6","uuid":"743683d4-2b36-4fec-955d-b8f68b632dc5","timestamp":"2026-05-21T11:59:58.930Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T110541/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '放弃 ''temporal instability as primary finding'' framing。Reframe\n  为 methodological contribution paper： (1) Semi-synthetic validation framework (ΔFPR=0.000)\n  升级为 primary contribution； (2) Ground truth meta-critique 升级为 co-primary contribution；\n  (3) Temporal DIF findings 降级为 motivating example / case study； (4) Audit protocol\n  重新定位为 ''proposed workflow''。 Title 改为类似 ''Validating Item-Level Contamination Detection:\n  A Semi-Synthetic Framework with Cross-Subject Matching''。 仍冲 EMNLP methodology track，但需要\n  substantially 重写 intro/framing。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,219 models × 12,508 items) 上的 MH-DIF\n    分析，含 temporal/ability cohort、within-family confound control、domain-specificity\n  expected_results:\n    temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n    temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.32\n    temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n    ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n    ability_enrichment: 1.19\n    within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n    within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct: 38.7\n    domain_spearman_rho: 0.38\n    domain_spearman_p: 0.004\n    sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n    temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n    irt_lz_above_2_pct: 98.0\n  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，31.3% C% 本身可复现但被 reviewer 视为 artifact。核心攻击点： (1) domain_spearman_rho=0.38\n    (p=0.004) 比 best 档预期的 0.25-0.30 更高，reviewer 用此论证 DIF 主要捕捉 domain-level capability\n    improvement 而非 item instability； (2) within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% 被解读为 \"DIF\n    在测 generation gap\"——Llama-2 到 Llama-3 是 architecture + scale + data 全面升级，61% DIF\n    恰恰说明 DIF 在测能力提升； (3) enrichment=0.96 ≈ 1.0 被解读为 DIF 与任何已知 contamination signal\n    无关——\"你的方法跟 contamination 没关系，它只是在找 hard items that newer models solve\"； (4) IRT\n    |Lz|>2 at 98% 被解读为 conditioning variable (total score) 根本不适合 MMLU—— MH 依赖 total\n    score 做 ability matching，但 57-subject multidimensional structure 使 total score\n    成为 poor proxy，整个 DIF 分析的 conditioning 基础被质疑。 random split 0.18% 只证明 temporal signal\n    存在，不证明 signal = instability。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 1: DIF Classification by Cohort Definition'\n    columns:\n    - cohort\n    - n_ref\n    - n_foc\n    - pct_A\n    - pct_B\n    - pct_C\n    - enrichment_li\n    rows:\n    - - temporal_2023v2024\n      - 1253\n      - 656\n      - 48.2\n      - 20.5\n      - 31.3\n      - 0.96\n    - - ability_quintile\n      - 1044\n      - 1044\n      - 89.8\n      - 7.3\n      - 2.9\n      - 1.19\n    - - random_split_control\n      - 950\n      - 950\n      - 97.3\n      - 2.5\n      - 0.18\n      - 1.01\n  - title: 'Table 2: Within-Family DIF (Confound Control)'\n    columns:\n    - family_pair\n    - n_ref\n    - n_foc\n    - pct_C\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Llama-2_vs_Llama-3\n      - 161\n      - 308\n      - 61.3\n      - generation gap drives DIF\n    - - Mistral_vs_Mixtral\n      - 89\n      - 142\n      - 38.7\n      - architecture shift contributes\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1: Domain-level C% vs accuracy improvement scatter (ρ=0.38, p=0.004)。Reviewer\n    会标注 regression line 并论证正相关说明 DIF tracks capability gain。'\n  - 'Fig 2: |Lz| distribution — 98% above 2.0 的 histogram，作为 IRT misfit 的 visual evidence。'\n  analysis: 'Worst-tier reviewer 的核心论证链：domain ρ=0.38 → within-family 61% → enrichment≈1.0\n    → IRT 98% misfit → 结论是 \"DIF 在 MMLU 上不是 item instability detector，而是 capability\n    gap detector， 你的 31% 就是在说 models got better on 31% of items\"。这个攻击路径在逻辑上是 self-consistent\n    的， 即使 item-level decomposition 只解释 2.4pp——reviewer 会说 domain-level predictor 是\n    wrong granularity， 真正的 confound 是 item-level difficulty × model generation interaction。\n\n    '\n- name: rl_robustness_validation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: DIF 对 RL 训练模型的鲁棒性验证：alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, N=477) + reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO,\n    N=10-15)\n  expected_results:\n    alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct: 29.8\n    alignment_rl_jaccard_vs_temporal: 0.72\n    reasoning_rl_n_models: 13\n    reasoning_rl_added_to_focal_c_pct: 30.5\n    reasoning_rl_jaccard_vs_base_focal: 0.85\n    delong_p_dif_vs_constat: 0.23\n    delong_p_dif_vs_mink: 0.18\n    tost_equivalence_p: 0.08\n    constat_auroc_non_rl: 0.74\n    constat_auroc_rl: 0.68\n    mink_auroc_non_rl: 0.71\n    mink_auroc_rl: 0.63\n    dif_auroc_across_compositions: 0.61\n    partial_exploitation_detection_boundary_p: 0.55\n    bootstrap_ci_width_auroc: 0.15\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验有两个致命问题： (1) N=13 reasoning-RL models 使所有统计检验 underpowered——DeLong\n    test p=0.23 和 TOST p=0.08 都不显著，reviewer 正确指出 \"你无法区分 DIF 对 RL 鲁棒 vs 你没有足够样本检测差异\"；\n    (2) DIF AUROC=0.61 本身就低——reviewer 论证 MH-DIF 在 any cohort composition 下 detection\n    power 都不 competitive，不是 RL-robust 而是 uniformly weak； (3) ConStat 和 Min-K% 在 RL\n    上的 degradation (0.74→0.68, 0.71→0.63) 比预期温和， 不足以构成 \"traditional methods fail on\n    RL\" 的 strong claim。 Bootstrap CI width=0.15 在 13 个模型上是预期内的，但 reviewer 会说这个宽度下任何\n    claim 都是 preliminary。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Detection AUROC by Method × Model Type'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - non_rl_auroc\n    - alignment_rl_auroc\n    - reasoning_rl_auroc\n    - delta\n    rows:\n    - - MH-DIF\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.6\n      - -0.02\n    - - ConStat\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.68\n      - -0.06\n    - - Min-K%\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.69\n      - 0.63\n      - -0.08\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Power curve — DIF detection TPR vs exploitation rate p ∈ [0.4, 1.0]，标注 detection\n    boundary at p=0.55。Reviewer 会指出 boundary 太高——half the contaminated items need\n    to be exploited before detection kicks in。'\n  analysis: '在 worst 档 reframing 中，此实验被降级甚至 drop。N=13 的 RL 验证无法支撑任何 robust claim。\n    如果 reviewer 看到 DIF AUROC=0.61 且 bootstrap CI=[0.54, 0.76]，会质疑 \"为什么要用 detection\n    power 这么低的方法\"。Reframed paper 中应将此实验移入 appendix 作为 preliminary evidence， 或完全 drop\n    并在 limitations 中说明。\n\n    '\n- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003a\n  description: ConStat-style perturbation testing 在 MMLU 上的独立评估：200+ items LLM paraphrasing\n    + FDR-controlled detection\n  expected_results:\n    n_items_reformulated: 220\n    constat_fdr_controlled_detections: 45\n    constat_detection_rate: 0.205\n    constat_fpr_estimate: 0.08\n    constat_auroc_non_rl: 0.74\n    constat_auroc_rl: 0.68\n    constat_dif_overlap_jaccard: 0.15\n    paraphrase_quality_score: 0.82\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下，ConStat detection rate=20.5% 在 non-RL 模型上是 reasonable\n    baseline， 但 DIF-ConStat overlap Jaccard=0.15 极低——reviewer 论证两种方法在测不同的东西， ensemble\n    前提不成立。ConStat 的 AUROC=0.74 > DIF 的 0.62，reviewer 会问 \"既然 ConStat 更准，为什么不直接用 ConStat？DIF\n    的 added value 在哪里？\" 更致命的是，ConStat 在 RL 上只 degradation 6pp (0.74→0.68)， 不够 dramatic\n    来支撑 \"traditional methods fail on RL\" 的 narrative。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Venn diagram of DIF-C flags vs ConStat detections，Jaccard=0.15 的极低 overlap\n    被 reviewer 用来论证两种方法在测完全不同的 construct。'\n  analysis: '此实验在 worst 档的 reframed paper 中价值有限。如果 DIF 被降级为 case study， ConStat comparison\n    也失去 anchor。可以保留为 \"related methods comparison\" 但不再是核心 contribution。\n\n    '\n- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003b\n  description: DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上的独立评估：10-15 open-weight models × 50\n    responses/item\n  expected_results:\n    n_models_evaluated: 12\n    n_items_scored: 1200\n    dvd_bimodal_detection_rate: 0.12\n    dvd_auroc: 0.65\n    dvd_dif_overlap_jaccard: 0.11\n    dvd_constat_overlap_jaccard: 0.22\n    verbatim_vs_variant_dvd_gap: 0.18\n  result_rationale: 'DVD detection rate=12% 低于 ConStat 的 20.5%，AUROC=0.65 处于 poor-to-fair\n    区间。 DVD-DIF overlap Jaccard=0.11 甚至低于 ConStat-DIF 的 0.15——三种方法之间的 agreement 极低，reviewer\n    论证 \"这些方法在测量三个不同的东西，没有一个是 validated contamination signal\"。 N=12 模型的 generation\n    variance 采样也不足以覆盖 model diversity。 在 worst 档下，DVD 的弱结果进一步削弱了 ensemble 的 rationale。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'DVD 在 worst 档下是 net negative——弱结果被 reviewer 用来论证 contamination detection\n    整个 paradigm 的 fragility。建议在 reframed paper 中 drop 此实验。\n\n    '\n- name: ensemble_fusion\n  plan_id: plan_003c\n  description: DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号融合：calibrated thresholds + 2-of-3 voting + weighted\n    fusion\n  expected_results:\n    ensemble_2of3_coverage: 0.38\n    ensemble_2of3_fpr: 0.12\n    ensemble_weighted_auroc: 0.72\n    ensemble_vs_best_single_auroc_gain: -0.02\n    cross_val_weight_stability_cv: 0.35\n    uniform_vs_optimized_auroc_gap: 0.03\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 ensemble 的核心问题是 base signal quality 太低。三种方法 pairwise\n    Jaccard 全部 <0.25，2-of-3 voting 的 agreement 稀少导致 coverage=38% 但 FPR=12% (超过 0.10\n    target)。 weighted fusion AUROC=0.72 竟然低于 ConStat standalone 的 0.74——ensemble 反而\n    hurt performance。 cross-validation weight stability CV=0.35 表明 weights 在 fold\n    间不稳定，reviewer 正确指出 \"你的 ensemble 在 overfitting fold-specific patterns\"。 这个实验在 original\n    framing (Claim 2: ensemble detection) 下是 fatal negative， 是 paper framing pivot\n    的直接原因之一。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Ensemble vs Individual Signal Performance'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - auroc\n    - fpr_at_80recall\n    - coverage\n    rows:\n    - - DIF (MH)\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.31\n    - - ConStat\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.21\n    - - DVD\n      - 0.65\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.12\n    - - Ensemble (2-of-3)\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.38\n    - - Ensemble (weighted)\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.42\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Ensemble 在 worst 档下是 paper 的最大 sunk cost。三信号 low-agreement + ensemble\n    ≤ best single = reviewer 一句话 kill：\"the whole is less than its parts\"。Reframed\n    paper 必须完全 drop Claim 2 (ensemble)，将 plan_003a/b/c 全部移入 \"future work\"。\n\n    '\n- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: GSM8K 上的 DIF 复制 + GSM1K ground truth correlation + semi-synthetic validation\n  expected_results:\n    gsm8k_temporal_c_pct: 18.9\n    gsm8k_external_c_pct: 47.4\n    gsm8k_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n    semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n    semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_p05: 0.42\n    gsm1k_n_models: 33\n    gsm1k_pearson_r: -0.478\n    gsm1k_spearman_rho: -0.403\n    gsm1k_direction: NEGATIVE\n    gsm1k_partial_r: -0.385\n    gsm1k_permutation_p: 0.014\n    gsm1k_ci_upper_r: -0.16\n    gsm1k_ci_upper_rho: -0.03\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验有一个 devastating result：GSM1K correlation 方向是 NEGATIVE\n    (r=-0.478)—— DIF-C items 与 contamination gap 反相关。Reviewer 的解读：\"DIF 标记的 items 恰恰是\n    2024 模型 genuinely improved 的 items（不需要 contamination），而真正 contaminated 的 items\n    不被 DIF 检测到，因为 contamination 是 uniform across cohorts\"。 这直接支持了 worst 档的核心假设——DIF\n    在测 ''models got better'' 而非 contamination。 N=33 虽小但方向一致 (permutation p=0.014)，CI\n    upper bound |r|=0.16 也远离 positive territory。 Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=0.42 at p=0.5\n    落在 worst 档范围 [0.3, 0.5] 内，被视为 \"moderate 但不 compelling\"——p=0.5 意味着一半 contaminated\n    models 必须 exploit item 才能检测到。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: GSM1K Contamination Gap vs DIF Flag Correlation'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - ci_lower\n    - ci_upper\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - pearson_r\n      - -0.478\n      - -0.71\n      - -0.16\n      - 0.005\n    - - spearman_rho\n      - -0.403\n      - -0.67\n      - -0.03\n      - 0.02\n    - - partial_r_controlling_acc\n      - -0.385\n      - -0.65\n      - -0.04\n      - 0.027\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Scatter plot of per-model DIF-C item accuracy vs GSM1K gap，negative slope。Reviewer\n    会把这张图作为 ''DIF ≠ contamination'' 的 smoking gun。'\n  analysis: 'GSM1K negative correlation 是 worst 档最有力的 ammunition。在 reframed paper\n    中必须 将此结果 reinterpret 为 \"DIF and contamination measure orthogonal constructs\"——\n    这 actually supports Claim 2 (ground truth meta-critique) 而不是 undermines it。 Key\n    reframing: \"DIF measures differential item functioning, not contamination per\n    se. The negative GSM1K correlation confirms that item-level behavioral change\n    ≠ contamination signal, validating our meta-critique that web-overlap labels are\n    fundamentally mismatched.\"\n\n    '\n- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: MMLU bifactor IRT 模型拟合 + anchor item 选择 + fixed-parameter calibration\n    equating pilot\n  expected_results:\n    bifactor_convergence: false\n    bifactor_rmsea: 0.089\n    bifactor_cfi: 0.72\n    bifactor_tli: 0.68\n    bifactor_srmr: 0.11\n    general_factor_explained_variance_pct: 28.4\n    n_anchor_items_selected: 0\n    equating_feasible: false\n    computation_time_hours: 18.5\n    convergence_code: iteration limit reached\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 bifactor 模型 fails to converge on 12,508 × 5,219 矩阵。\n    即使强制截断 iterations，fit indices 全部不达标 (RMSEA=0.089 > 0.06 cutoff, CFI=0.72 < 0.90\n    cutoff, TLI=0.68)。General factor 仅解释 28.4% variance， 说明 MMLU 的 57-subject structure\n    导致 essentially 无法用 single general factor 建模。 这直接验证了 reviewer 的 IRT misfit concern——不只是\n    |Lz| 的问题，连 bifactor 都 fail， 说明 MMLU 在 IRT 框架下 fundamentally ill-behaved。 结果：equating\n    pipeline 被 kill，anchor items 无法选择，plan_006 (item generation) 也被 block。 这个 negative\n    result 在 reframed paper 中反而有价值——motivates future multidimensional IRT work。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Scree plot showing 57 eigenvalues with no dominant first factor — visual\n    evidence of MMLU''s irreducible multidimensionality。'\n  analysis: 'Bifactor failure 是 plan_005/006/008 整条 pipeline 的 kill signal。在 reframed\n    paper 中 列入 limitations：\"IRT-based equating requires adequate model fit; MMLU''s\n    57-subject multidimensional structure defeats both unidimensional and bifactor\n    specifications. This motivates future work on multidimensional IRT or subject-specific\n    calibration.\"\n\n    '\n- name: item_generation_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: DIF-flagged MMLU items 的 LLM 替换生成 + student simulation calibration\n  expected_results:\n    n_items_generated: 0\n    difficulty_correlation_prompt: null\n    difficulty_correlation_simulation: null\n    calibration_feasible: false\n    blocked_by: plan_005_bifactor_failure\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验被 plan_005 failure 完全 block。没有可靠的 IRT 参数估计和 anchor\n    items， 生成的替换 items 无法 calibrate 到 equated scale 上。即使独立运行 prompt-based generation，\n    已有文献 (arXiv 2602.06631) 表明 difficulty correlation 仅 ρ=0.10-0.45， 而 student simulation\n    需要先有 IRT 参数才能 simulate——circular dependency。 整个 regeneration pipeline (original\n    Claim 3) 被 kill，是 paper pivot 的主要 driver 之一。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Not executed。在 reframed paper 中完全 drop，不出现在 main body 或 appendix。 Original\n    Claim 3 (regeneration) 已被 bifactor failure 否定。\n\n    '\n- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: Sinharay et al. (2006) cumulative Bayesian DIF priors 的 simulation\n    study：4 successive administrations\n  expected_results:\n    individual_admin_tpr_delta10: 0.42\n    cumulative_2admin_tpr: 0.55\n    cumulative_3admin_tpr: 0.63\n    cumulative_4admin_tpr: 0.68\n    target_tpr_070: false\n    individual_admin_tpr_delta14: 0.58\n    fpr_all_below_010: true\n    prior_sensitivity_max_tpr_swing: 0.09\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 cumulative power improvement 存在但低于 target：3-admin 后\n    TPR=0.63 < 0.70 target， 4-admin 才到 0.68。Reviewer 批评这是 pure simulation：\"你没有 4 个\n    time period 的真实数据， 这只是说 ''if we had more data, DIF would work better''——tautological。\"\n    更关键的是，simulation 使用 well-specified 1D IRT model，而真实 MMLU 的 IRT misfit (98%) 意味着\n    simulation results 不 transferable。\"你在模拟一个你已经证明不存在的世界。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Cumulative DIF Power by Number of Administrations'\n    columns:\n    - n_admin\n    - delta_10_tpr\n    - delta_14_tpr\n    - delta_16_tpr\n    - fpr\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.04\n    - - 2\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.05\n    - - 3\n      - 0.63\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.05\n    - - 4\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.83\n      - 0.89\n      - 0.06\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Simulation-only + IRT misfit = reviewer 完全 dismiss。在 reframed paper 中移入\n    appendix 或 drop。Methodology track reviewer 可能 appreciate the framework 但会要求 real\n    data validation。\n\n    '\n- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Benchmark validity degradation under progressive item replacement (5%–50%)\n  expected_results:\n    replacement_5pct_rho: 0.999\n    replacement_10pct_rho: 0.998\n    replacement_20pct_rho: 0.996\n    replacement_50pct_rho: 0.988\n    replacement_5pct_shr: 0.993\n    replacement_10pct_shr: 0.991\n    replacement_20pct_shr: 0.987\n    replacement_50pct_shr: 0.972\n    construct_coverage_maintained_at_20pct: true\n    blocked_by_equating: true\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验 partially blocked by plan_005 failure (无法用 equated\n    replacement items)。 可以用 random replacement 做 simulation，结果显示极高 robustness (ρ>0.988\n    even at 50% replacement)。 但 reviewer 将此解读为 MMLU 的 massive redundancy 的进一步证据： \"你可以\n    drop 一半的 items 且 ranking 不变——这说明 MMLU 有 6000+ redundant items， 你的 31% DIF finding\n    完全在 redundancy margin 内，没有任何实际影响。\" 讽刺的是，robustness 越高，DIF findings 的 practical\n    significance 越低。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Ranking Stability Under Progressive Item Replacement'\n    columns:\n    - replacement_pct\n    - spearman_rho\n    - shr\n    - construct_coverage_ratio\n    rows:\n    - - 5\n      - 0.999\n      - 0.993\n      - 0.98\n    - - 10\n      - 0.998\n      - 0.991\n      - 0.96\n    - - 20\n      - 0.996\n      - 0.987\n      - 0.93\n    - - 50\n      - 0.988\n      - 0.972\n      - 0.85\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Degradation curve — ρ vs replacement % 几乎是 flat line until 50%。Reviewer\n    用此图论证 ''DIF findings are practically irrelevant''。'\n  analysis: '在 reframed paper 中，graceful degradation 反而支持 revised narrative： \"MMLU''s\n    massive redundancy means DIF-flagged items can be safely removed without validity\n    loss — the diagnostic value of DIF is in understanding WHAT changed, not in removing\n    items for quality control。\" 但 worst 档 reviewer 会说 \"如果 removal 没有影响，你的 whole paper\n    的 motivation 就不成立。\"\n\n    '\n- name: item_focused_trees\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger 2016) 作为 continuous-covariate DIF\n    替代方案\n  expected_results:\n    ift_n_items_dif: 3452\n    ift_c_pct_equivalent: 27.6\n    ift_mh_concordance: 0.78\n    ift_split_point_median_date: 2023-09\n    ift_gradual_items_pct: 62.3\n    ift_abrupt_items_pct: 37.7\n    ift_computation_time_hours: 8.2\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 IFT 的 continuous treatment 暴露了 temporal DIF 的 gradual\n    nature： 62.3% 的 DIF items 显示 gradual difficulty drift 而非 abrupt change。 Reviewer\n    用此论证 \"这是 models gradually getting better on certain items， 不是 contamination event\n    或 structural instability——difficulty drift 是 capability improvement 的自然结果，你的 binary\n    2023/2024 split 人为制造了 abrupt 的假象。\" Split point median at 2023-09 也不 informative——没有对应任何\n    specific model release event。 IFT-MH concordance=0.78 表明 MH 的 binary grouping\n    丢失了 22% 的 nuance。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: IFT vs MH-DIF Classification Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - MH_DIF\n    - IFT\n    - concordance\n    rows:\n    - - n_flagged_items\n      - 3918\n      - 3452\n      - 0.78\n    - - pct_C_equivalent\n      - 31.3\n      - 27.6\n      - '-'\n    - - gradual_vs_abrupt\n      - N/A (binary)\n      - 62.3% / 37.7%\n      - '-'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Item difficulty trajectories for 20 representative DIF items showing gradual\n    monotonic drift — reviewer 用此 visual 论证 ''this is just learning curves, not instability''。'\n  analysis: 'IFT 在 worst 档下是 double-edged sword：提供了 finer-grained picture 但 picture\n    说的是 \"gradual improvement\" 而非 \"instability\"。Reframed paper 中可以保留为 robustness check\n    并 reframe：\"IFT confirms that item-level behavioral changes are predominantly gradual,\n    consistent with progressive capability development rather than discrete contamination\n    events。\"\n\n    '\n- name: architecture_stratified_dif\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: Decoder-only 子群上的 DIF 分析 + IRT fit diagnostics\n  expected_results:\n    n_decoder_only: 5226\n    n_non_decoder: 1\n    pct_decoder_only: 99.98\n    decoder_only_c_pct: 31.3\n    decoder_only_jaccard_vs_full: 1.0\n    irt_rmsea_full: 0.082\n    irt_rmsea_decoder_only: 0.081\n    irt_cfi_full: 0.74\n    irt_cfi_decoder_only: 0.74\n    irt_lz_above_2_pct_decoder_only: 97.8\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下此实验 trivially resolves architecture concern (99.98% decoder-only,\n    removing 1 model changes nothing, Jaccard=1.0) 但 completely fails to address IRT\n    misfit。RMSEA 从 0.082→0.081, CFI unchanged at 0.74——IRT misfit 不是 architecture\n    heterogeneity 造成的，而是 MMLU 57-subject multidimensionality 造成的。 Reviewer：\"你证明了 architecture\n    不是问题，但 IRT misfit 依然是 98%—— 移除 1 个 encoder model 不可能解决 57-subject 的 multidimensionality\n    问题。 你需要的是 multidimensional IRT 或 per-subject analysis，不是 architecture stratification。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: IRT Fit Diagnostics — Full vs Decoder-Only'\n    columns:\n    - population\n    - N\n    - RMSEA\n    - CFI\n    - TLI\n    - pct_Lz_above_2\n    rows:\n    - - full\n      - 5227\n      - 0.082\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.71\n      - 98.0\n    - - decoder_only\n      - 5226\n      - 0.081\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.71\n      - 97.8\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '此实验在 worst 档下是 necessary but trivially resolved。不提供任何 defense against\n    IRT misfit concern。在 reframed paper 中一句话带过：\"99.98% of METABENCH models are decoder-only;\n    architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue (Jaccard=1.0)\"。 IRT misfit 需要在 limitations\n    中 honestly address 而非 dismiss。\n\n    '\n- name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: Known contamination injection into METABENCH matrix + DIF detection\n    power measurement\n  expected_results:\n    temporal_external_tpr_p0: 0.326\n    temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.45\n    temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.42\n    temporal_external_tpr_p07: 0.78\n    temporal_external_tpr_p10: 0.95\n    temporal_external_fpr: 0.314\n    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.35\n    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.62\n    cross_subject_delta_fpr: 0.0\n    within_subject_fpr_inflation: 0.186\n    ability_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.302\n    standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10: 0.318\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 semi-synthetic 的 ΔTPR at p=0.5 = 0.35，落在 worst 范围 [0.3,\n    0.5] 下半区。 Reviewer 的攻击： (1) \"ΔTPR=0.35 at p=0.5 意味着在 half exploitation 下你只比 baseline\n    多检测 35% 的 contaminated items——这在 practical terms 下意味着你漏掉了大部分 contamination\"； (2)\n    \"Baseline FPR=0.314 意味着你的 detector 在没有 injection 时已经 flag 31.4% 的 items 作为 positive——这要么是\n    FPR 不可接受，要么是你的 ''clean'' items 并不 clean， 无论哪种解读都 undermine 你的 validation\"； (3)\n    \"Cross-subject matching 的 ΔFPR=0.000 是 technically impressive 但 semantically questionable——你用\n    other subjects 的 score 做 matching variable，这意味着你在用 math ability 来 match science\n    items，matching variable 和 target variable 的 construct relevance 未验证\"。 但在 reframed\n    paper 中，这个实验反而是最 defensible 的——reviewer 攻击的是 interpretation 而非 methodology，cross-subject\n    matching ΔFPR=0.000 是 hard empirical fact。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Semi-Synthetic Validation — DIF Detection Power'\n    columns:\n    - exploitation_rate_p\n    - tpr\n    - delta_tpr\n    - fpr\n    - delta_fpr\n    rows:\n    - - 0.0\n      - 0.326\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.0\n    - - 0.3\n      - 0.45\n      - 0.124\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.0\n    - - 0.5\n      - 0.676\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.0\n    - - 0.7\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.454\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.0\n    - - 1.0\n      - 0.95\n      - 0.624\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Dose-response curve — ΔTPR vs exploitation rate p，cross-subject matching\n    (ΔFPR=0.000) vs within-subject matching (FPR inflation)。这是 reframed paper 的 centerpiece\n    figure。'\n  analysis: 'Semi-synthetic validation 是 worst 档 reframing 的 primary contribution。\n    虽然 ΔTPR=0.35 at p=0.5 不 impressive，但 (1) cross-subject ΔFPR=0.000 是 novel methodological\n    contribution，(2) dose-response monotonicity 证明 framework 有效， (3) within vs cross\n    matching comparison 是 actionable guidance。 Reframed paper 应强调 framework reusability\n    而非 specific detection performance。\n\n    '\n- name: multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\n  plan_id: plan_028\n  description: 6 个 benchmark (MMLU/ARC/HellaSwag/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA/GSM8K) 上的 temporal\n    DIF 分析\n  expected_results:\n    mmlu_c_pct: 31.3\n    winogrande_c_pct: 30.3\n    truthfulqa_c_pct: 29.7\n    arc_c_pct: 26.9\n    gsm8k_c_pct: 18.9\n    hellaswag_c_pct: 17.9\n    cross_benchmark_range: 17.9-31.3%\n    all_random_controls_below_1pct: true\n    min_enrichment_ratio: 45\n    n_benchmarks: 6\n    cross_benchmark_mean_c_pct: 25.8\n    cross_benchmark_sd_c_pct: 5.8\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 6-benchmark consistency (C%=17.9-31.3%, all >45× above\n    random) 被 reviewer 反转利用。核心论证：\"所有 6 个 benchmark 都显示 high DIF 恰恰证明这是 method artifact，\n    不是 benchmark-specific instability。如果 DIF 在测 item instability，不同 benchmark 应该有不同的\n    instability profile——HellaSwag (commonsense) 和 GSM8K (math) 的 instability 机制完全不同。但\n    C% 的 cross-benchmark consistency (mean=25.8%, SD=5.8%) 说明 DIF 在 uniformly 捕捉 ''temporal\n    cohort difference'' 的 statistical signal， 而这个 signal 就是 ''models got better''。\"\n    更具体地：HellaSwag 和 GSM8K 的 C% 较低 (17.9%, 18.9%) 恰好是 capability improvement 最 saturated\n    的 benchmarks (HellaSwag accuracy >90%, GSM8K has clear skill ceiling)， 而 MMLU\n    (31.3%) 和 WinoGrande (30.3%) 的 C% 较高恰好是 improvement space 最大的 benchmarks。 这个 pattern\n    与 \"DIF = capability improvement\" 假说 perfectly consistent。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Cross-Benchmark Temporal DIF Summary'\n    columns:\n    - benchmark\n    - n_items\n    - n_ref\n    - n_foc\n    - pct_C\n    - random_pct_C\n    - enrichment_ratio\n    rows:\n    - - MMLU\n      - 12508\n      - 1080\n      - 807\n      - 31.3\n      - 0.18\n      - 174\n    - - WinoGrande\n      - 1267\n      - 1017\n      - 803\n      - 30.3\n      - 0.32\n      - 95\n    - - TruthfulQA\n      - 817\n      - 1080\n      - 807\n      - 29.7\n      - 0.37\n      - 80\n    - - ARC-Challenge\n      - 1172\n      - 1080\n      - 807\n      - 26.9\n      - 0.6\n      - 45\n    - - GSM8K\n      - 1319\n      - 1017\n      - 804\n      - 18.9\n      - 0.3\n      - 63\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - 10042\n      - 1080\n      - 807\n      - 17.9\n      - 0.28\n      - 64\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Bar chart of C% across 6 benchmarks with random control overlay。Reviewer\n    会标注 ''all bars above 15% — uniform artifact'' annotation。'\n  - 'Fig: C% vs benchmark mean accuracy (2024 cohort)，negative correlation 暗示 saturation\n    effect。'\n  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark 一致性在 worst 档下是 double-edged sword。在 original framing\n    下 支持 generalizability；在 worst 档下被解读为 method artifact。 Reframed paper 中应 reinterpret：\"Cross-benchmark\n    consistency confirms that temporal cohort design reliably detects DIF across diverse\n    benchmarks, whether the signal represents item instability, capability improvement,\n    or both. Our semi-synthetic framework can disambiguate this — we demonstrate this\n    on MMLU and GSM8K。\"\n\n    '\n- name: permutation_null_c_rate\n  plan_id: plan_029\n  description: 1000× permutation test：randomly reassign temporal labels → MH-DIF →\n    null C% distribution\n  expected_results:\n    n_permutations: 1000\n    null_c_pct_mean: 0.22\n    null_c_pct_sd: 0.08\n    null_c_pct_95th: 0.38\n    null_c_pct_99th: 0.48\n    observed_c_pct: 31.3\n    permutation_p: <0.001\n    effect_size_z: 388.5\n    null_matches_random_split: true\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 permutation null C%=0.22% (SD=0.08%)，observed 31.3%\n    极显著高于 null (z=388, p<0.001)。但 reviewer 的反应不是 \"impressive\" 而是 \"so what\"： \"当然 31.3%\n    above chance——你在比较 2023 vs 2024 models，它们 obviously different。 任何 test 都会 reject\n    the null that these groups are exchangeable。 这个 permutation test 只证明 temporal\n    signal exists，不证明 signal = item instability 而非 capability improvement。你需要的不是 ''is\n    31% above chance'' 而是 ''is 31% above what capability improvement alone would produce''——而后者正是你的\n    decomposition analysis (plan_019) 和 matching analysis (plan_027) 试图回答但未完全回答的问题。\"\n    Permutation null ≈ random split control (0.18% vs 0.22%)，consistent， 但这个 consistency\n    也只是说明两种 null 都 measure the same thing (label exchangeability)。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Permutation Null Distribution Summary'\n    columns:\n    - statistic\n    - value\n    rows:\n    - - observed_C_pct\n      - 31.3\n    - - null_mean\n      - 0.22\n    - - null_SD\n      - 0.08\n    - - null_95th_percentile\n      - 0.38\n    - - z_score\n      - 388.5\n    - - permutation_p\n      - <0.001\n    - - random_split_control\n      - 0.18\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Null C% distribution histogram (1000 permutations) with observed 31.3% marked\n    as extreme outlier。Visually compelling 但 reviewer 会 annotate ''proves temporal\n    signal, not item instability''。'\n  analysis: 'Permutation test 在 worst 档下 necessary but not sufficient。Establishes\n    that temporal labels carry real signal (not random)，但 signal identity 仍 contested。\n    在 reframed paper 中保留为 one-paragraph validation： \"Permutation test confirms C%=31.3%\n    is not a statistical artifact of the MH procedure (null: 0.22±0.08%, p<0.001)。Decomposition\n    of the temporal signal into item-level vs cohort-level components is addressed\n    by plan_019 and plan_027。\"\n\n    '\n- name: odds_ratio_regression_transparency\n  plan_id: plan_030\n  description: DIF flag 的 odds ratio regression：domain-level → item-level predictors\n    + Simpson's paradox 分析\n  expected_results:\n    model1_mcfadden_r2: 0.0007\n    model1_nagelkerke_r2: 0.0012\n    model1_subject_acc_delta_or_per_010: 1.55\n    model1_subject_acc_delta_ci:\n    - 1.19\n    - 2.03\n    model2_mcfadden_r2: 0.0423\n    model2_subject_acc_delta_or_per_010: 0.73\n    model2_ctt_difficulty_or: 0.78\n    model2_discrimination_or: 1.51\n    model3_item_delta_or_per_010: 1.08\n    model3_mcfadden_r2: 0.0012\n    model4_mcfadden_r2: 0.0434\n    model4_item_acc_change_or: 0.92\n    model4_discrimination_or: 1.54\n    simpsons_paradox: true\n    simpsons_or_flip: 1.55 → 0.73\n    lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2: 646.98\n    lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2: 655.53\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 Simpson''s paradox (OR 1.55→0.73) 被 reviewer 反转利用。 核心论证：Model\n    1 (domain accuracy delta only) 显示 OR=1.55——domain 进步越大，DIF 越多， 看似支持 \"DIF tracks\n    capability improvement\"。但加入 item-level properties (difficulty, discrimination)\n    后 OR flips to 0.73——controlling for item properties，domain improvement REDUCES\n    DIF probability。 Reviewer 的解读：\"Simpson''s paradox 证明 item-level properties (difficulty,\n    discrimination) 才是 DIF 的 true driver，domain improvement 只是 ecological confound。\n    你的 DIF 方法在挑出 high-discrimination, moderate-difficulty items——这些恰好是 区分好模型和差模型的\n    items，它们 ''show DIF'' 不是因为 instability 而是因为它们 discriminate well，而 2024 models\n    恰好比 2023 models 好。\" Discrimination OR=1.51-1.54 across all models 是最 consistent\n    predictor—— higher discrimination → more likely DIF。这直接支持了 worst 档的核心假设： DIF 在\n    measure ''items that separate good from bad models'' 即 ''models got better''。\n    McFadden R²=0.043 虽然 low in absolute terms，但 Model 1→Model 2 的 LR test χ²=647\n    (p≈0) 说明 item properties 是 massively significant predictors。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Logistic Regression Models Predicting DIF-C Classification'\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - predictors\n    - mcfadden_r2\n    - nagelkerke_r2\n    - aic\n    - key_or\n    rows:\n    - - M1\n      - subject_acc_Δ\n      - 0.0007\n      - 0.0012\n      - 15545\n      - 1.55 [1.19,2.03]\n    - - M2\n      - subject_acc_Δ + difficulty + discrimination\n      - 0.0423\n      - 0.072\n      - 14902\n      - 0.73 (acc_Δ), 1.51 (disc)\n    - - M3\n      - item_acc_Δ\n      - 0.0012\n      - 0.0021\n      - 15537\n      - 1.08 [1.03,1.14]\n    - - M4\n      - item_acc_Δ + difficulty + discrimination\n      - 0.0434\n      - 0.074\n      - 14885\n      - 0.92 (acc_Δ), 1.54 (disc)\n  - title: 'Table: Simpson''s Paradox — OR Flip Summary'\n    columns:\n    - predictor\n    - model1_or\n    - model2_or\n    - direction_flip\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Domain acc Δ (per 0.10)\n      - 1.55\n      - 0.73\n      - positive→negative\n      - confounded by item properties\n    - - Item acc Δ (per 0.10)\n      - 1.08\n      - 0.92\n      - positive→negative\n      - confounded by item properties\n    - - CTT discrimination (per 0.10)\n      - '-'\n      - 1.51\n      - consistent positive\n      - true driver\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Forest plot of ORs across 4 models — visual display of Simpson''s paradox\n    flip。Reviewer 会用此图作为 ''DIF = discrimination artifact'' 的 key evidence。'\n  - 'Fig: Partial dependence plot — DIF probability vs discrimination，showing monotonic\n    increase。'\n  analysis: 'Simpson''s paradox 在 worst 档下是 most damaging single result。Reviewer 论证链：\n    discrimination drives DIF → high-discrimination items separate cohorts → 2024\n    cohort is better → DIF flags items where 2024 models outperform 2023 models BECAUSE\n    those items have high discrimination → \"DIF is measuring item quality, not instability\"。\n    在 reframed paper 中需要 carefully reinterpret： \"The OR flip reveals that item-level\n    properties, particularly discrimination, are the proximal predictors of DIF classification.\n    This is psychometrically expected: high-discrimination items magnify any ability\n    difference between groups, producing larger MH odds ratio shifts. The question\n    is whether this represents (a) genuine item instability amplified by discrimination,\n    or (b) stable items faithfully discriminating between cohorts of different ability.\n    Our decomposition evidence (ability confound ≤2.4pp, plan_027) supports interpretation\n    (a), but we acknowledge this remains the central interpretive challenge。\"'\n","numLines":942,"startLine":1,"totalLines":942}}}
